# Task 9 — QW embedding e2e real episodes.db (f6-p0-quickwins-nightbench)

Date: 2026-08-21
Scope: crates/kitty-memory/** ONLY (kitty-harness lane untouched)

## 1. Test `embedding_blob_migration_and_recall` (crates/kitty-memory/src/embedding.rs)

Upgraded from NamedTempFile smoke to full e2e against a REAL sqlite file:

- DB: `<tempdir>/episodes.db` created via `EpisodeStore::open` — NEVER the live
  `~/.kitty/episodes.db` (tempdir only; asserted in code comment).
- Production schema semantics: `EpisodeStore::open` now sets
  `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` + `PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000` right after
  `Connection::open`, matching Catalyst apohara-episodic/store.rs:68 pattern.
  Test probes a second raw connection and asserts journal_mode == "wal".
- Session 1: insert 6 episodes WITH 384-dim embedding BLOBs
  (`save_with_embedding`). Target inserted FIRST (oldest) so recency cannot
  explain top-1. Embeddings are deterministic splitmix64 random unit vectors
  (network-free; no fastembed model download in tests).
- Session 2: drop store (clean WAL shutdown) → reopen same file = migration
  path over existing table; `ensure_embedding_column` duplicate-column no-op;
  count preserved; blake3 content hash stable across reopen and equal to
  recomputed `Episode::compute_hash`; BLOB roundtrip exact.
- Recall: `recall_hybrid(paraphrased_query, Some(&query_emb), 3)` with query
  "websocket gateway drops connection intermittently" vs target goal "fix
  flaky websocket reconnect loop in gateway service" → assert top-1 id ==
  target.id and goal contains "websocket". Comment in test states hybrid is
  NOT asserted superior in general — losing honestly is acceptable.

## 2. blake3 incremental deltas

episodic.rs computes blake3 for episode id/hash only. NO incremental blake3
delta path for embeddings exists → skipped silently per task spec (nothing
invented). The migration test covers the existing blake3 id/hash path across
close/reopen instead.

