## 4. Recall comparison — HONEST REPORTING (synthetic, NOT a product metric)

Harness: benches/ab_recall.py run as-is (script has NO --limit flag; it is a
fixed 12-query fixture). This is the SYNTHETIC toy corpus (12 handcrafted
episodes, 3-dim toy embeddings constructed so hybrid wins) — explicitly NOT a
product metric and not labeled as one anywhere in this deliverable.

Numbers as measured:
- Hybrid RRF k=60 top-1 correct: 12/12 queries
- Jaccard top-1 correct: 2/12 queries
- Strict win (hybrid top-1 correct AND Jaccard not): 10/12 = 83.3%
- Lenient win (hybrid rank better): 12/12 = 100.0%
- Script verdict: PASS 83.3% > 60% threshold; RRF sanity OK

Honesty caveats published with these numbers:
- Fixture is synthetic and hybrid-favorable by construction; these numbers
  must never be quoted as product recall.
- Hybrid losing to lexical on real data remains an acceptable outcome; no
  merge gate depends on hybrid winning.

